# Docker build context = repo root. Keep it small and free of secrets.
# The AWS CDK reads this file too when it packages the images.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
packages/db/src/generated
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The CDK app is a workspace member, so `turbo prune` needs its package.json. Its code and
# cdk.out stay out: infrastructure edits then don't change the images' hash (no rebuild).
infra/cdk/*
!infra/cdk/package.json
